<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lustrātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		lustro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a purification by sacrifice, a lustration</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lustrationis sacro peracto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					40, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">40, 13, 2</span></i>
			sq.; <i><span class="en">Col.
				2, 22, 5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> [v. lustro, II.], <i>a
				going</i> or <i>wandering about</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lustrationesque (ferarum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 27, 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">municipiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 2, 23, 57</span></i>
			.</div>
